@startuml http_result_bean_compatibility
title ResultBeanAdapter Standalone and Company Replacement

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 8691e8800f05f28afe22499050c29220ef5b7475):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/result/ResultBeanAdapter.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/result/StandaloneResultBeanAdapter.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Observed behavior: controllers depend on ResultBeanAdapter and standalone code provides the approved JSON shape.
' Java divergence: the internal ResultBeanFactory artifact is not available in the standalone repository.
' Design reason: company code replaces one Spring bean without inventing an internal FQCN or duplicate class.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
package "Business source" {
  class "SessionController" as Controller
  class "RuntimeApiExceptionHandler" as Handler
}

interface "ResultBeanAdapter" as Contract
class "StandaloneResultBeanAdapter\nresCode, resMsg, result" as Standalone
class "Company ResultBeanAdapter Bean" as CompanyAdapter
class "Company ResultBeanFactory" as Company
class "Company Maven settings" as Settings

class "MessageSource\nen-US and zh-CN" as Messages

Controller --> Contract : normal(result)
Handler --> Contract : error(code, message)
Handler --> Messages : resolve error code and arguments
Standalone ..|> Contract
CompanyAdapter ..|> Contract
CompanyAdapter --> Company : getFactory().normal(result)
Settings --> Company : resolves artifact

note bottom of Contract
Standalone builds do not define a fake company FQCN.
Internal coordinates, repository URLs, credentials, and unverified methods
remain outside the public repository.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_dual_authentication
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 21c3f59be033e7bdd5506a2d9d48baa2581bc3c7):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/
' RuntimeEventController.java: submit; RuntimeRequestContext.java: mateCredentials.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/
' HttpMateToolClient.java: invokeTool, queryToolIdsByAgentId, queryToolIdsBySkillId, queryToolMetaByIds.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/dto/RequestHeaderInfo.java: toHeaders.
' Observed behavior: four headers are captured; RuntimeEventService.requireCredentials still rejects incomplete values.
' Pending implementation: remove local checks in the entry, CallMateTool.execute, and HttpMateToolClient.invokeTool.
' Product constraint: context headers are optional; POST Events and Command may include access-token.
' Header scope evidence (pi-mono-java 53eff85c7f41de23eb434e027782f5085a8b8e45):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java: submit.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/service/command/CommandExecutionService.java: executeBuiltin.
' Observed behavior: only user.message consumes new event credentials; Builtin retains its internal invocation lifetime.
' Design reason: callers provide execution credentials only for new messages and Skill, not control/read/configuration calls.
' Security hardening: keep received values only in one execution snapshot and never persist or log them.
' Security boundary: discovery, model, and other calls are credential-free; only Mate execute forwards
' the received X-HW-ID, Authorization, X-HW-APPKEY, and access-token values without renaming.
' Presentation: one responsibility-level scenario; implementation details remain in the linked document.
